.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt IRQ_ACK 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm irq_ack
.Nd acknowledge a device interrupt
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn irq_ack irq
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm re-enables a level-triggered
.Dv LEGACY
line after the driver has acknowledged the interrupt at the device.
The line is also unmasked on the first
.Nm
before any interrupt fired.
For
.Dv MSI
and
.Dv MSIX
the call is the driver's quiesce barrier: it reports that the driver handled
the last firing and disabled the source in the device (for example by
clearing the MSI enable bit).
A live MSI source closed without a final
.Nm
cannot be proven quiet, so the kernel quarantines its vector permanently
instead of handing it to a new
.Em Irq .
An MSI object that was never waited on is treated as inert and may release
its vector immediately.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Fa irq
is not an interrupt handle.
.It Er EACCES
The handle lacks the
.Dv READ
right.
.El
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
